></mml:math></disp-formula></p></sec><sec><title>Pre-publication history</title><p>The pre-publication history for this paper can be accessed here:</p><p><ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://www.biomedcentral.com/1472-6890/8/12/prepub"/></p></sec><sec sec-type="supplementary-material"><title>Supplementary Material</title><supplementary-material content-type="local-data" id="S1"><caption><title>Additional file 1</title><p><bold>Bland-Altman plot including 95% limits of agreement between adjusted calcium by the previously published equation and adjusted calcium by the locally derived equation (Note: mean difference = 0.09, 95% limits of agreement: 0.043 to 0.136, units = mmol/L).</bold> Abbreviations: Adj. = Adjusted.</p></caption><media xlink:href="1472-6890-8-12-S1.doc" mimetype="application" mime-subtype="msword"><caption><p>Click here for file</p></caption></media></supplementary-material></sec></body><back><ack><sec><title>Acknowledgements</title><p>Mathew James is supported by fellowship awards from the Kidney Research Scientist Core Education Training Program and the Alberta Heritage Foundation for Medical Research. Brenda Hemmelgarn is supported by a New Investigator Award from the Canadian Institutes of Health Research and a Population Health Investigator Award from the Alberta Heritage Foundation for Medical Research.</p></sec></ack><ref-list><ref id="B1"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Payne</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Little</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Williams</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Milner</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Interpretation of serum calcium in patients with abnormal serum proteins</article-title><source>Br Med J</source><year>1973</year><volume>4</volume><fpage>643</fpage><lpage>646</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">4758544</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B2"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Orell</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Albumin as an aid to the interpretation of serum calcium</article-title><source>Clin Chim Acta</source><year>1971</year><volume>35</volume><fpage>483</fpage><lpage>489</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">5125334</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/0009-8981(71)90224-5</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B3"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Berry</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Gupta</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Turner</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Burns</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Variations in plasma calcium with induced changes in plasma specific gravity, total protein and albumin</article-title><source>Br Med J</source><year>1973</year><volume>4</volume><fpage>640</fpage><lpage>643</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">4758543</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B4"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Payne</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Carver</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Morgan</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Interpretation of serum total calcium: effects of adjustment for albumin concentration on frequency of abnormal values and on detection of change in the individual</article-title><source>J of Clin Path</source><year>1979</year><volume>32</volume><fpage>56</fpage><lpage>60</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">429580</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1136/jcp.32.1.56</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B5"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Ashby</surname><given-names>J</given-names